WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.160
Nora runs a small parcel studio.

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:06.485
She asks her AI helper
to prepare a shipping label.

3
00:00:06.624 --> 00:00:10.400
The helper sees a button, chooses a click,
and the app carries it out.

4
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.464
But a panel has just moved.

5
00:00:12.464 --> 00:00:14.470
The click lands somewhere else.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.540
The mouse moved successfully.

7
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.350
The label was not prepared.

8
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.530
A computer-using AI doesn’t finish a task

9
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.350
just by describing a click.

10
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.296
In one common design, the application
sends it a picture of the screen.

11
00:00:28.436 --> 00:00:31.596
The model chooses
a mouse or keyboard action.

12
00:00:31.596 --> 00:00:35.250
The application runs that action
and returns the result.

13
00:00:35.576 --> 00:00:37.569
Then the agent has to look again.

14
00:00:37.819 --> 00:00:40.479
Our studio turns that loop
into three stations.

15
00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:42.369
Look. Act. Check.

16
00:00:42.619 --> 00:00:45.339
The check matters,
because a page can scroll,

17
00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:48.400
a panel can open,
or the screen can change.

18
00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:52.080
The documentation for Claude’s
computer use tool says Claude

19
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.139
sometimes assumes an action
worked without checking,

20
00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:58.149
and suggests a fresh screenshot
after each step.

21
00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:01.999
Some web agents read the page’s elements
instead of pictures.

22
00:01:01.999 --> 00:01:03.800
The lesson is the same.

23
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.463
Verify the result, rather than assume it.

24
00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:10.203
Nora doesn’t accept a moving cursor
as a finished label.

25
00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.107
She checks the actual draft
and its status.

26
00:01:13.247 --> 00:01:15.687
If the result is missing or unclear,

27
00:01:15.687 --> 00:01:19.357
the helper should stop,
look at the current screen, and replan,

28
00:01:19.357 --> 00:01:21.577
not blindly repeat the same click.

29
00:01:21.827 --> 00:01:24.877
Before you trust a business agent,
ask three things.

30
00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:27.320
What did it see?
What did it actually do?

31
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.937
And what proves the result?

32
00:01:29.187 --> 00:01:32.527
Keep consequential actions
behind a separate approval.

33
00:01:32.527 --> 00:01:34.337
The goal isn’t more clicking.

34
00:01:34.337 --> 00:01:35.777
It’s a checked result.

35
00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:37.607
Ahmadreza Samadi.

36
00:01:37.607 --> 00:01:39.544
